    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d382">

                <pb facs="0766" n="646" xml:id="pg646"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">824.51/107: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Cottrell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">La
                                Paz</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-05-16T15:00:00-04:32"><hi rendition="#italic">May 16, 1922—3
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received May 23—5:35 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>18. Chamber of Deputies yesterday passed bill in approximate form desired by New
                    York bankers authorizing immediate loan of $19,000,000 also additional
                    $4,000,000 as needed for completion Potosi-Sucre railway. Bill also provides
                    that bonds held by Ulen Contracting Corporation be refunded and consolidated
                    with new loan making total amount $33,000,000. Of this sum $24,000,000 are to be
                    offered to public immediately and additional $9,000,000 within next 2 years.</p>
                <p>Little opposition looked for in the Senate where bill is expected to pass this
                        week.<anchor n="6" xml:id="d382-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cottrell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d382-f1" n="6" xml:id="d382-f1-content">
                <p>The loan law was promulgated by President Saavedra, May 24.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
